            block("Inspect", "Look for feeding at dusk or after rain, slime trails, ragged leaf edges, eggs and damage to seedlings.", "Check leaf undersides, stems and the soil surface; photograph the damage and note the date.", "Also check for water stress, wind damage, overcrowding and disease, which can look like pest damage."),
            block("Reduce losses", "Protect young plants with physical barriers or collars that fit securely and do not trap wildlife.", "Remove hiding places immediately around vulnerable seedlings and keep the bed easy to inspect.", "Choose control methods appropriate to the pest and follow the product label and Irish rules. Avoid unlabelled homemade chemical mixtures.", "For an uncertain or serious problem, compare symptoms with Teagasc advice or ask a qualified horticultural adviser."),
